-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §20 דרגות קידום: a teacher under the reform
-- accrues credit points — for a role held a whole year (from תשע"ב), and
-- for being among the best 30% evaluated in his school (from תשע"ג) — and
-- every 10 points bring a promotion grade of 2% of the combined salary
-- alone, three years apart at least and four at most; what the supplement's
-- base holds, what it counts for, and the cumulative table.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`

§ `20 דרגות קידום`

-- The opening: a teacher employed on the reform's terms may accrue credit
-- points, from the start of that employment on, toward a promotion-grade
-- supplement, as (א)–(יא) set out.
@ref akn:art_20/p1
GIVEN e IS A `extent of the Oz reform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may accrue credit points` e IF
    NOT e EQUALS `off the Oz reform`

§§ `20(א)`

-- (א)(1), from תשע"ב: a teacher who holds one of the roles listed for a
-- whole school year, at a reasonable level, earns the points beside it.
-- The list is closed (convention reading.closed-list): the deputy
-- principal, the educational counsellor and the teacher given tasks earn
-- none for their role.
@ref akn:art_20__para_a akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_1/t1
GIVEN r IS A `Oz role`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the credit points for the role` r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the Oz grade coordinator` THEN 4
    WHEN `the Oz social-education coordinator` THEN 3
    WHEN `the Oz subject coordinator` THEN 3
    WHEN `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator` THEN 2.5
    WHEN `the Oz adjustments coordinator` THEN 2.5
    WHEN `the Oz trips coordinator` THEN 2.5
    WHEN `the Oz homeroom teacher` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0

-- (א)(2): a teacher holding more than one role in a school year earns the
-- points of one only, the role that gives the most.
@ref akn:art_20__para_a__subpara_2
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      roles IS A LIST OF `Oz role`
      `held the whole year at a reasonable level` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the role points of the year` y roles `held the whole year at a reasonable level` IS
    IF y AT LEAST `the school year 5772` AND `held the whole year at a reasonable level`
    THEN maximum (0 FOLLOWED BY map `the credit points for the role` roles)
    ELSE 0

§§ `20(ב)`

-- (ב), from תשע"ג (teachers who began on the reform's terms in תשע"ב
-- too): the teachers whose evaluation (by §19's model) is the highest in
-- their school in a school year earn points — 30% of the school's teachers,
-- in three bands of 10%. A teacher is in a band when his place in the
-- ranking is within its share of the school's teachers, counted exactly
-- (convention rounding.default: a share is not rounded to whole teachers),
-- and teachers with equal results share a place (convention
-- thresholds.ties).
@ref akn:art_20__para_b akn:art_20__para_b/p2 akn:art_20__para_b/p3
GIVEN `teachers evaluated above him` IS A NUMBER
      `the school's teachers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the evaluation band` `teachers evaluated above him` `the school's teachers` IS
    BRANCH
        IF place AT MOST 10% TIMES `the school's teachers` THEN 1
        IF place AT MOST 20% TIMES `the school's teachers` THEN 2
        IF place AT MOST 30% TIMES `the school's teachers` THEN 3
        OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        place MEANS `teachers evaluated above him` PLUS 1

-- The table: a column for the homeroom teacher, one for the grade,
-- subject, evaluation, adjustments, social-education and trips
-- coordinators, one for "a teacher who is not a role holder".
DECLARE `column of section 20(ב)'s table` IS ONE OF
    `the homeroom teachers' column`
    `the coordinators' column`
    `the column of a teacher who is not a role holder`

@ref akn:art_20__para_b/t1
GIVEN c IS A `column of section 20(ב)'s table`, band IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the evaluation points in` c band IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `the homeroom teachers' column` THEN
        BRANCH IF band EQUALS 1 THEN 3
               IF band EQUALS 2 THEN 2
               IF band EQUALS 3 THEN 1
               OTHERWISE 0
    WHEN `the coordinators' column` THEN
        BRANCH IF band EQUALS 1 THEN 2
               IF band EQUALS 2 THEN 1
               IF band EQUALS 3 THEN 0.5
               OTHERWISE 0
    WHEN `the column of a teacher who is not a role holder` THEN
        BRANCH IF band EQUALS 1 THEN 4
               IF band EQUALS 2 THEN 3
               IF band EQUALS 3 THEN 2
               OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN r IS A `Oz role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a coordinator the table names` r IF
        r EQUALS `the Oz grade coordinator`
    OR r EQUALS `the Oz subject coordinator`
    OR r EQUALS `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator`
    OR r EQUALS `the Oz adjustments coordinator`
    OR r EQUALS `the Oz social-education coordinator`
    OR r EQUALS `the Oz trips coordinator`

-- The columns as printed: a homeroom teacher's, the six coordinators', and
-- a teacher with no role at all.
GIVEN roles IS A LIST OF `Oz role`
GIVETH A LIST OF `column of section 20(ב)'s table`
DECIDE `the columns the table prints for` roles IS
    append (IF elem `the Oz homeroom teacher` roles THEN LIST `the homeroom teachers' column` ELSE EMPTY)
           (append (IF any `a coordinator the table names` roles THEN LIST `the coordinators' column` ELSE EMPTY)
                   (IF null roles THEN LIST `the column of a teacher who is not a role holder` ELSE EMPTY))

-- F-oz-founding-20-a: the columns leave out a role holder whose role is in
-- neither — the deputy principal, the educational counsellor, the teacher
-- given tasks, the holder of another role — and give two to a homeroom
-- teacher who coordinates. The reading adopted (convention
-- reading.analogy): any other role holder is in the coordinators' column,
-- that of the role holders who are not homeroom teachers; and a teacher in
-- two columns earns the more, as (א)(2) does for roles.
GIVEN roles IS A LIST OF `Oz role`
GIVETH A LIST OF `column of section 20(ב)'s table`
DECIDE `the columns a teacher's roles put him in` roles IS
    IF null roles OR NOT null (`the columns the table prints for` roles)
    THEN `the columns the table prints for` roles
    ELSE LIST `the coordinators' column`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      roles IS A LIST OF `Oz role`
      `teachers evaluated above him` IS A NUMBER
      `the school's teachers` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the evaluation points of the year` y roles `teachers evaluated above him` `the school's teachers` IS
    IF y AT LEAST `the school year 5773`
    THEN maximum (0 FOLLOWED BY map (GIVEN c YIELD `the evaluation points in` c band) (`the columns a teacher's roles put him in` roles))
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        band MEANS `the evaluation band` `teachers evaluated above him` `the school's teachers`

§§ `20(ג)`

-- (ג): the points are due at the end of the school year in which the role
-- was held or for which the evaluation was given: 31 August, the school
-- year being from 1 September (convention dates.school-year).
@ref akn:art_20__para_c
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day the points are due for school year` y IS
    DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 (y PLUS 1)

§§ `20(ד)–(ז)`

-- (ד): a teacher who accrues 10 points is entitled, from the day he is
-- entitled to them, to a promotion-grade supplement of 2% of the combined
-- salary (alone). (ה): no percentage or shekel supplement is in its base,
-- those that count toward percentage supplements on the combined salary
-- among them.
@ref akn:art_20__para_d akn:art_20__para_e
`the points a promotion grade takes` MEANS 10
`the rate of a promotion grade` MEANS 2%

GIVEN grades IS A NUMBER, `the combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the promotion-grade supplement for` grades `the combined salary` IS
    `the rate of a promotion grade` TIMES grades TIMES `the combined salary`

-- (ו): the supplement is in the base of no percentage supplement. (ז): it
-- counts for the hour value, severance pay, and contributions to a pension
-- provident fund, a training fund and the Dafna fund.
@ref akn:art_20__para_f akn:art_20__para_g
GIVEN p IS A `what an Oz salary component counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the promotion-grade supplement counts for` p IF
    NOT `computing a percentage supplement` p

§§ `20(ח)–(י)`

-- (ח): on the day a teacher is entitled to a grade he starts accruing
-- anew, from zero; points beyond the 10 do not count toward the next.
-- (ט): a further grade waits until three years at least have passed since
-- the last ("לפחות": 3 is in); points accrued meanwhile stay until it is
-- due. (י): four grades at most in a teacher's employment in the upper
-- divisions. Points are due at the end of a school year ((ג)), so years
-- are counted in school years. The rule takes the points due at the end of
-- each school year, from the first.
@ref akn:art_20__para_h akn:art_20__para_i akn:art_20__para_j
`the most promotion grades` MEANS 4
`the school years between promotion grades at least` MEANS 3

GIVEN `this school year` IS A NUMBER
      `the points of each year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `points accrued` IS A NUMBER
      grades IS A NUMBER
      `the year of the last grade` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the promotion grades from` `this school year` `the points of each year` `points accrued` grades `the year of the last grade` IS
    CONSIDER `the points of each year`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN grades
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF      total AT LEAST `the points a promotion grade takes`
            AND waited
            AND grades LESS THAN `the most promotion grades`
        THEN `the promotion grades from` (`this school year` PLUS 1) rest 0 (grades PLUS 1) (JUST `this school year`)
        ELSE `the promotion grades from` (`this school year` PLUS 1) rest total grades `the year of the last grade`
        WHERE
            total MEANS `points accrued` PLUS p
            waited MEANS CONSIDER `the year of the last grade`
                         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                         WHEN JUST last THEN `this school year` MINUS last AT LEAST `the school years between promotion grades at least`

GIVEN `the first school year` IS A NUMBER
      `the points of each year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the promotion grades earned` `the first school year` `the points of each year` IS
    `the promotion grades from` `the first school year` `the points of each year` 0 0 NOTHING

§§ `20(יא)`

-- (יא), "for the avoidance of doubt": the cumulative rate of the
-- supplement at each entitlement.
@ref akn:art_20__para_ja akn:art_20__para_ja/t1
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cumulative promotion-grade rate (יא) prints at entitlement` n IS
    BRANCH IF n EQUALS 1 THEN 2%
           IF n EQUALS 2 THEN 4%
           IF n EQUALS 3 THEN 6%
           IF n EQUALS 4 THEN 8%
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `20 -- illustrations`

-- (יא)'s table is (ד)'s rate, grade on grade
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `the cumulative promotion-grade rate (יא) prints at entitlement` n EQUALS `the rate of a promotion grade` TIMES n) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4)
#ASSERT `the promotion-grade supplement for` 2 10000 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the role points of the year` `the school year 5772` (LIST `the Oz homeroom teacher`, `the Oz grade coordinator`) TRUE EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the role points of the year` `the school year 5772` (LIST `the Oz deputy principal`) TRUE EQUALS 0
-- 25 teachers: places 1–2 are the top band, 3–5 the next, 6–7 the last
#ASSERT `the evaluation band` 1 25 EQUALS 1 AND `the evaluation band` 2 25 EQUALS 2 AND `the evaluation band` 6 25 EQUALS 3 AND `the evaluation band` 7 25 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the evaluation points of the year` `the school year 5773` EMPTY 0 25 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the evaluation points of the year` `the school year 5772` EMPTY 0 25 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the evaluation points of the year` `the school year 5773` (LIST `the Oz homeroom teacher`, `the Oz subject coordinator`) 0 25 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT NOT `the promotion-grade supplement counts for` `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`
#ASSERT `the promotion-grade supplement counts for` `contributions to the Dafna fund`
-- a grade coordinator (4) with top evaluations as one (2): 6 points a year
-- reach 10 in the second year; the next waits three years; four at most
#ASSERT `the promotion grades earned` `the school year 5773` (LIST 6, 6) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the promotion grades earned` `the school year 5773` (LIST 6, 6, 6, 6) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the promotion grades earned` `the school year 5773` (LIST 6, 6, 6, 6, 6) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the promotion grades earned` `the school year 5773` (LIST 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the day the points are due for school year` `the school year 5773` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 8 2013

-- F-oz-founding-20-a's evidence: as printed, a deputy principal is in no
-- column and a homeroom teacher who coordinates a subject in two.
`section 20(ב)'s columns do not part the teachers` MEANS
        null (`the columns the table prints for` (LIST `the Oz deputy principal`))
    AND null (`the columns the table prints for` (LIST `the Oz educational counsellor`))
    AND count (`the columns the table prints for` (LIST `the Oz homeroom teacher`, `the Oz subject coordinator`)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `section 20(ב)'s columns do not part the teachers`
